WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.316
Use the total electron density at 0.0248 electrons per cubic bohr on a 112³

00:00:10.316 --> 00:00:14.000
grid. Enable electrostatic potential mapping.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.667
Use a symmetric color range of ±0.130 hartree per electron charge. Changing

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.000
this range recolors the same shell.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.789
The completed mesh contains 21,064 triangles. The density isovalue sets the

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:34.000
shell geometry and the potential sets its color.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.947
The Phong export retains the numeric potential bar and the molecular

00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:46.000
framework. The figure records what the colors mean.
